write('REVIEW.md','''# Four complete original marked-ideal operation helpers: draft only

The complete fixed-4c6 source and every selected doc/type/proof are captured. Their parent source is byte-identical at fixed47cef. The original Algebra context precedes product/power monotonicity; its original closing ends those variables. The original Controlled context, including the unused nu binder, precedes the two controlled-transform theorems. Its closing and the final anonymous noncomputable/namespace closings are all retained. No later MarkedIdeal namespace declaration is copied.

Only the frozen namespace/open relocation, release header and pure imports are administrative. The four whole statement/proof chunks remain byte-identical. The existing ControlledProductTransformExact import genuinely supplies the already-public isCoherent_D and controlled-transform uniqueness imports; the old partial parent supplies idealPow_idealPow, mul_sumIdeal and pullback_sumIdeal. Their actual base metadata owners are recorded.

The product proof maps actual span generators; the power proof recursively uses it, including power zero. The two controlled-transform proofs retain original coherence and whole centre-power hypotheses and use the genuine original uniqueness/factor identities; no desired transform identity is assumed. Two complete original blueprint lemma nodes with both full written proofs are captured. The first directly attaches all four declarations; the second is contextual and is not a claim that its unselected statements have been exported. Inherited native ready markers are historical, not new local acceptance.

The already-approved actual-CI metadata/edge captures are reused, not rerun. There are no additional ordinary original callees outside the actual public base and these four. The recursive power theorem also generates its original _f wrapper, which is retained as compiler diagnostic metadata rather than a fifth handwritten theorem.

No production Lean or BP file, old source/artifact, Git state or runtime was changed. Separate complete peer, frontier integration, actual build/kernel/type/value/owner/axiom/binding gates remain pending.
''')
